# Vauxhall Vectra C saloon, 2002-2008.
#
# The last Vectra: the larger car on the Epsilon platform with the Signum
# hatchback variant, sold from March 2002 and replaced by the Insignia in
# 2008. The saloon is modelled; the hatchback, estate and Signum are not
# separately represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vauxhall_Vectra
#
# Dimensions 4.596 x 1.798 x 1.460 m, wheelbase 2.700 m.
#
# Shape reference: NO true level side elevation exists. Image 1 is a front
# three-quarter about 25 degrees off, so the flank is estimated within the
# published dimensions and the limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no Vauxhall colour list was read. White, Red, Blue and
# Silver are plain names. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39, provisional.
#
# Speed 200 km/h. Comfort 80/450, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 80. Classes 0,1,2.
# Dates: intro March 2002; retires staggered 2014-2017 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-vectra-c.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vauxhall-vectra-c.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-vectra-c/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the pre-facelift UK saloon is modelled. NO true level
# side elevation was available, so the flank stations are estimated from
# oblique photographs within the published dimensions. The facelift nose, the
# rear wiper and the tow bar are not modelled.


obj=citycar
name=VauxhallVectraC(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=2002
intro_month=3
retire_year=2017
retire_month=6
speed=200
class=0,1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=80
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=450

Image[E]=./images/vauxhall-vectra-c-white_E.0.0,-33,14
